body:
This is happening in libtermkey, `driver-ti.c:lookup_next`.

@sittim If you are running a local build, any chance you could try reverting https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/5758 ? Also, you didn't mention your `$TERM`. Is `$TERM` empty?

@leonerd Any hints about this? Is this most likely a bug on our end? I've never seen this before.

@justinmk Oooh wow. I've never seen that one before.
That sounds possibly a bug in libtermkey. That's some very odd behaviour of its terminfo-based string parsing code. On first glance of the code I can't possibly imagine how it can get into that state (which is why it SIGABRTs; that's supposed to be impossible).

@sittim: Some more detail might be helpful here - can we get a copy of the full output of `infocmp -L` on the terminal in question? That would give us all the TI key strings.
